# The theme for a terminal with a light background.  Copy it to make another (NAME.theme in this directory: `nch --theme NAME`).
# One style per line: its name, then any of fg=, bg=, weight=bold|normal|dim, underline=yes|no, italic=yes|no,
# reverse=yes|no (foreground and background swapped).
# A colour is #rrggbb, terminal (the terminal's own), or one of the sixteen of the terminal's palette (red, bright-red ...).
# What a style leaves out it keeps from the style around it; what default leaves out is the terminal's own.

default
em      fg=#000000  weight=bold
hide    fg=#9e9e9e
good    fg=#2e7d32
bad     fg=#c62828
warn    fg=#b45309
select  fg=#1f5fbf
cmd     fg=#5b3fbf
pkg     fg=#2f5f8f
file    fg=#4a4a7a

# alt: every other row of a table that asks for it (the fields of `nch packages NAME`), in the alt version of each
# style (alt for plain text); for now each looks as the style it stands for.
alt
alt-em     fg=#000000  weight=bold
alt-hide   fg=#9e9e9e
alt-good   fg=#2e7d32
alt-bad    fg=#c62828
alt-warn   fg=#b45309
alt-select fg=#1f5fbf
alt-cmd    fg=#5b3fbf
alt-pkg    fg=#2f5f8f
alt-file   fg=#4a4a7a
